/target

# Loose binaries left next to the source by a stray `cargo build` invocation or
# a copied-out executable. The real build output lives in /target.
*.exe
*.pdb

# Identity token the client writes when it is run without --name, so a player
# returns to the same slot after a restart. Local to one machine.
.orewar-token

# The server and name last connected to, so the connect screen opens on them
# next time. Local in the same way.
.orewar-connect

# A second checkout kept alongside this one to build for another architecture.
# Its sources are a copy; the 2 GB is its own target/, which /target above does
# not reach because that pattern is anchored to the repository root.
/orewar_arm
